    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        What actually helps
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Sunscreen, every morning.</strong> Dermatologists say that effective care for dark marks begins with sunscreen, and a review of treatments for post-inflammatory hyperpigmentation found that almost every study recommended SPF 30 or higher.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34525885/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a> If marks linger, tinted sunscreen with iron oxide adds protection against visible light.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32335182/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Niacinamide.</strong> In trials in Japanese women, niacinamide decreased hyperpigmentation and increased skin lightness compared with a plain base after four weeks of use. One of those trials included 120 people with facial tanning.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12100180/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Time.</strong> Marks that are a few shades darker than your natural skin colour usually fade within 6 to 12 months once the cause is stopped, and deeper colour can take far longer.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        For marks that stay, the same review found the strongest evidence for retinoids, hydroxy acids and broad-spectrum sunscreen.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/34525885/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a> Retinoids and acids can irritate, so they are worth discussing with a dermatologist before you start.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        A simple routine after sun exposure
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        If your skin is red, hot or peeling after sun, let it settle before adding an active. Once it is comfortable, a short routine is enough:
    </p>

    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Cleanse</strong> with a gentle cleanser.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;"><strong>Apply 3 to 4 drops of a pigment-focused serum on damp skin.</strong></li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;"><strong>Moisturise.</strong></li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Wear sunscreen every morning,</strong> and reapply if you are outdoors for long.</li>
    </ol>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        <a href="/products/dark-spots-pore-control-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Dark Spots, Pore Control Serum</a> is built for this step. It combines niacinamide, kojic acid, vitamin C and five ceramides with Centella asiatica, and it works as the one active step in the routine. In the serum's own clinical study on 36 Indian women aged 24 to 44, with twice-daily use, 100% of patients improved dark spots in 8 weeks. Individual results may vary. Patch test before first use, and check with a doctor first if you are pregnant or breastfeeding.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:34px 0;padding:24px 26px;border-top:1px solid #B87330;border-bottom:1px solid #B87330;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 7px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;">Keep in mind</p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            Sunscreen is the step that decides whether the other steps work. A pigment serum can fade marks, and a single unprotected afternoon can bring them back.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Tan remedies compared
    </h2>

